{"id":"bath-sheba-bathsheba","name":"Bath-Sheba (Bathsheba)","aliases":["Bath-Sheba"],"sources":["nave","easton"],"topics":["nave:bath-sheba-bathsheba"],"groups":[],"definition":{"source":"easton","term":"Bath-sheba","text":"Daughter of the oath, or of seven, called also Bath-shu’a (1 Chr. 3:5), was the daughter of Eliam (2 Sam. 11:3) or Ammiel (1 Chr. 3:5), and wife of Uriah the Hittite. David committed adultery with her (2 Sam. 11:4, 5; Ps. 51:1). The child born in adultery died (2 Sam. 12:15-19). After her husband was slain (11:15) she was married to David (11:27), and became the mother of Solomon (12:24; 1 Kings 1:11; 2:13). She took a prominent part in securing the succession of Solomon to the throne (1 Kings 1:11, 16-21)."},"lemmas":[{"strong":"H1339","lemma":"בַּת־שֶׁבַע","xlit":"Bath-Shebaʻ","gloss":"Bath-Sheba, the mother of Solomon","kjv":"Bath-sheba","count":9,"share":0.26},{"strong":"H8010","lemma":"שְׁלֹמֹה","xlit":"Shᵉlômôh","gloss":"Shelomah, David's successor","kjv":"Solomon","count":12,"share":0.34},{"strong":"H138","lemma":"אֲדֹנִיָּה","xlit":"ʼĂdônîyâh","gloss":"Adonijah, the name of three Israelites","kjv":"Adonijah","count":8,"share":0.23},{"strong":"H113","lemma":"אָדוֹן","xlit":"ʼâdôwn","gloss":"sovereign","kjv":"lord, master, owner","count":9,"share":0.26},{"strong":"H3678","lemma":"כִּסֵּא","xlit":"kiççêʼ","gloss":"covered","kjv":"seat, stool, throne","count":7,"share":0.2},{"strong":"H5416","lemma":"נָתָן","xlit":"Nâthân","gloss":"Nathan, the name of five Israelites","kjv":"Nathan","count":5,"share":0.14}],"verses":["2Sam.11.3","1Kgs.1.11","1Kgs.1.15","1Kgs.1.16","1Kgs.1.28","1Kgs.1.31","1Kgs.2.13","1Kgs.2.18","1Kgs.2.19","2Sam.11.2","2Sam.11.4","2Sam.11.5","1Kgs.1.12","1Kgs.1.13","1Kgs.1.14","1Kgs.1.17","1Kgs.1.18","1Kgs.1.19","1Kgs.1.20","1Kgs.1.21","1Kgs.1.22","1Kgs.1.23","1Kgs.1.24","1Kgs.1.25","1Kgs.1.26","1Kgs.1.27","1Kgs.1.29","1Kgs.1.30","1Kgs.2.14","1Kgs.2.15","1Kgs.2.16","1Kgs.2.17","1Kgs.2.20","1Kgs.2.21","1Chr.3.5"],"related":[{